Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-03-2001||12:21 AM||||Ok, I have(will have) an 87gt auto 2.8(obviously) realllllly soon, what are my options to make it faster, off the line mainly, but I would like to see AT LEAST = power that my 85 gt does... Money is a factor in this, any help is great, thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||fropuff||11-03-2001||12:33 AM||||The main reason the '85 is faster than the '87 is because of the tranny.  Manual trans' are a bit faster, if you know how to drive them right.  As far as the auto tranny, I think shift kits help a little.  Gets rid of the long shifts.  Maybe a good tune-up would do a little, if it needs one.  Plugs, wires, clean injectors, etc.  Sorry, can't help too much.  Anyway: bump!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-03-2001||01:26 AM||||It's already got the same amount of power.  GM derated the '86-'88s on paper only for EPA purposes.  ||||reg||1
