Z||000005||jeffndebrus||11-03-2001||12:08 PM||||cheapest way would be to add pedals, a chain and sprocket.  There may be a kit available for $5,000-$10,000 but I believe you could do one up yourself with parts from Toysrus<BR>Enjoy trying! Have a nice day!||||reg||1
Z||000006||fastback87||11-04-2001||08:54 PM||||These answers are good and funny, but I am guessing that they don't really help this guy out much.  Or is it just me?  The best things you can do for cheap and quick "power" is change the tranny fluid and filter use sythetic fluid, change the oil I use Mobil 1, then port the exhaust.  I have done all of these and it has really helped mine 0-60 in &lt;7 sec.  I also don't like the idea of using original exhaust gaskets due to the fact that AutoZone doesn't stock them and they cost like $40, so I use (and have had better luck using) firebird gaskets they have bigger openings than my stock gaskets did, the gasket is smaller and easier to work with also.  You can do all of this yourself for under $50 and about a day of labor.  I also have an 87 GT with a 2.8 soon to have nitrous!!!!<P>Let me know if this helped more than the jokes.||||reg||12
Z||000007||fropuff||11-04-2001||09:13 PM||||fastback: do you really get a &lt;7 second 0-60 time?  If you do, I need to do some of that stuff.  I didn't think my answer was too bad.  Shift kits give get rid of the LONG smooth granny shifts.  Let me know if you get this time; it's good for $50.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||11-04-2001||09:28 PM||||Or, how about this...a shift kit, a new filter, new gasket, synthetic ATF, port the exhaust, clean the injectors, new plugs/wires if needed, donuts on all 4 corners.  How about that for 0-60?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||11-04-2001||09:29 PM||||wasn't me<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||fastback87||11-05-2001||01:19 AM||||Yes I really get this, but my engine also has the wrong cam in it and no donuts my tires are 215 60 15 Handles like it is on rails, just about as rough too. ;-)<P>by "Wrong Cam" I mean the cam is from the donor car of my engine (celebrity I think)<P>It is just barely under 7 and that is with a stop watch so it could be a little off.  But I noticed a big difference between the standard exhaust, conventional fluids and porting with fluid change to all synthetic.<P>Just my experience, maybe I am lucky...I don't have the shift kit though, where can I find one at a reasonable price?||||reg||1
Z||000011||avengador1||11-05-2001||10:22 PM||||Don't forget to put in a K&N filter and a free flow catalytic converter.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
